            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0310" n="190" xml:id="pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Higgins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-08T11:00:00-06:00">December 8, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>190. Reference first paragraph my telegram No. 188 of December 6 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">7</hi>], noon, Minister of Foreign Affairs has twice
                    again requested me to ascertain as soon as possible if Department will recognize
                    present government in Salvador. He is impatient for early information as his
                    Government’s action will be in conformity with that of the United States and he
                    is being strongly pressed to announce his Government’s decision.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Higgins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
